  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Question": "Express \\(1/x\\) and \\(1/(x+1)\\) with a common denominator.",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "\\(1/[x(x+1)]\\) and \\(1/[x(x+1)]\\)",
    "B": "\\((x+1)/[x(x+1)]\\) and \\(x/[x(x+1)]\\)",
    "C": "\\((x+1)/x\\) and \\(x/(x+1)\\)"
  },
  "Correct Answer": "B",
  "Accepted Answers": [],
  "Unordered Answers": false,
  "Solution": "The least common denominator is \\(x(x+1)\\). Multiplying both the numerator and denominator of \\(1/x\\) by \\(x+1\\) gives \\((x+1)/[x(x+1)]\\). Multiplying both the numerator and denominator of \\(1/(x+1)\\) by \\(x\\) gives \\(x/[x(x+1)]\\).",
